<title>BRAZIL: Ceval says in talks to sell soymeal to U.S. firm.</title>
<headline>Ceval says in talks to sell soymeal to U.S. firm.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian processor Ceval Alimentos said it was in talks to sell an unspecified amount of Brazilian soymeal to a U.S. firm but further details of the deal were not available.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a U.S. firm whom we are negotiating with at the moment to sell soymeal,&quot; a spokesman for Ceval said. &quot;We cannot reveal the identity of the firm until after the deal is closed.&quot;  </p>
<p>The deal was expected to be concluded in the next few days, he said. He did not know whether the agreement would involve one or more cargoes of meal.</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
